Subject: [PATCH v6 00/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:13:03 +0000

This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
the list's mail hub" [1] describes, on b/dev. It turns the relay jail
into the list's home in steps, one service at a time. Each step
leaves a jail that works and does what its README.org says.

How mail moves, end to end, once the series is applied:

  client --SMTP--> OpenSMTPD --LMTP--> Dovecot --Sieve--> lists
  Dovecot, every folder <--IMAP--> mbsync <--IMAPS--> Fastmail

Dovecot is the only program that writes the maildir. Once patch 10 is
applied, the maildir is a copy of the whole Fastmail account, INBOX
included, and mbsync syncs every folder both ways. Readers still see
only the list: the ACL lets an anonymous login list and read lists
and Archive, and no other folder.

- Patch 1 corrects the spec on what Dovecot does to a reader's write.
  A STORE or EXPUNGE answers OK and changes nothing; only append,
  copy, and move are refused. Acceptance step 7 now expects that.
- Patch 2 narrows the spec's header check to what OpenSMTPD does on
  its own: it refuses a header line that is neither a field nor a
  continuation, and on loopback adds a missing Message-ID and Date.
- Patch 3 makes Dovecot the only writer of the list. mbsync still
  fetches one way, but into Dovecot over IMAP as the login mbsync,
  not into the maildir. This is the one step that needs the maildir
  and mbsync's state emptied first.
- Patch 4 turns the fetch into a two-way sync of lists and Archive.
- Patch 5 adds Pat's login, so he can archive and delete on lab-mail.
- Patch 6 swaps smtprelay for OpenSMTPD, which hands posts to Dovecot
  over LMTP. smtprelay, jq, and the mailcred group go with it. Posts
  land in INBOX, since LMTP alone delivers only there.
- Patch 7 files each post into lists with a Sieve script from
  Pigeonhole, as the spec says, so mbsync carries it to Fastmail.
- Patch 8 documents the one-time import of the jj maildir.
- Patch 9 adds lab@lists.p7x.dev and freebsd-ports@lists.p7x.dev to
  the addresses OpenSMTPD delivers to the list. The Fastmail rule that
  files lab-devel@p7x.dev into lists must cover them too.
- Patch 10 syncs the whole account. INBOX moves into the maildir, so
  mbsync can sync it, and the ACL keeps readers to lists and Archive,
  since the account holds more than the list.

Before applying patch 10 on the running jail: a post that landed in
INBOX before Sieve was in place sits in /data/mail/dovecot/inbox,
which patch 10 leaves behind. Move it into lists from any IMAP client,
logged in as pat@p7x.dev, first. The first sync after patch 10 also
copies the rest of the account down from Fastmail, so it takes longer
than usual.

For every step I checked that each libexec script passes sh -n, and
that dist.mtree lists exactly the files under dist/. mbsync 1.5.1
parses the mbsyncrc of patch 10. Dovecot, smtpd, and the jail build
are not installed here, so no step was run. The ACL of patch 10 is
the part to check first on the jail. Outside lists and Archive, the
global ACL file names only Pat and mbsync, and no line for owner or
anyone. It relies on Dovecot then giving the owner, which every login
is, no rights there, not its default of every right. I could not
confirm that without Dovecot. If it is wrong, any reader could read
and change the whole account, so run acceptance step 7 before the
jail takes readers: it now checks that a reader's LIST shows only
lists and Archive and that it cannot SELECT INBOX.

Changes in v6:
- New patch 10 syncs the whole Fastmail account, not only lists and
  Archive, and limits readers to those two folders by ACL (Pat).
